1
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,370
- Enough already.
- What a hassle.

2
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:19,600
- Don't fight over the bed.
- What a hassle.

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,370
We just became teammates...

4
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:24,480
Stop it right now.

5
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,850
Look, the dust is flying everywhere!

6
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:28,090
Damn it.

7
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,009
Open the door to air it out.

8
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:36,900
Also, it's forbidden to carelessly
throw around towels and used clothes.

9
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,260
It's very annoying.

10
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:39,730
Okay.

11
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:42,400
I didn't know Barou was so tidy.

12
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,310
You're no king at all,

13
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:45,850
you're more like a servant.

14
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,940
Barou the Servant, making a grand entrance.

15
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,310
I really don't get along with you,

16
00:00:50,310 --> 00:00:52,310
Mr. Hassle.

17
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:54,450
What's with that weird nickname?
I don't like it.

18
00:00:54,450 --> 00:00:55,810
Go away, Mr. Hassle.

19
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:57,560
Don't call me that, my parents would cry.

20
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,530
Is that so.

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,500
For him, there are absolute personal rules

22
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,760
- I go to sleep at 22:00,
- and aesthetic values

23
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,710
- lights must be off.
- that could be considered mandatory?

24
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:09,840
A kind of strict self-disciplined lifestyle.

25
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:13,210
What a hassle, I just want to play games.

26
00:01:13,210 --> 00:01:16,190
Living together might really be a hassle,

27
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:18,640
but because of the aesthetic values
of personal rules,

28
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:21,510
different abilities emerge.

29
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:24,600
Maybe that's also the motivation
behind Barou's selfishness.

30
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,350
I want to understand Barou better.

31
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:30,060
I want to understand this person's true nature.

32
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:32,530
Barou, will you train with me later?

33
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,860
After we understand each other,

34
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,350
a chemical reaction will occur.

35
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:13,040
(Episode 16: The Three-Person Fusion)

36
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:18,060
We can train together,

37
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,730
but so far it's just the two of us training.

38
00:03:20,730 --> 00:03:22,590
What is he doing?

39
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:25,810
Seems like a physical workout
he has to do every day.

40
00:03:26,190 --> 00:03:27,270
It's been too long.

41
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:29,270
Besides, it's really tough.

42
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:31,850
Barou, how long are you going to train?

43
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,980
Hurry up and come train with us.

44
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:36,560
Wait another 40 minutes,

45
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,650
then I'll play with you.

46
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:40,060
I wonder

47
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:44,480
if he was already bad at socializing
since he was in the womb?

48
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:48,020
Waiting 40 minutes is enough time
to watch one drama episode.

49
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:51,270
If watching anime, about two episodes.

50
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:55,270
But, precisely because of this thorough
and consistent physical training,

51
00:03:55,270 --> 00:03:58,250
Barou can be so strong, right?

52
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:02,010
In a certain way, this is already abnormal.

53
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,680
Alright. If that's the case,

54
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,440
I'll join the training too.

55
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,730
Loser.

56
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:11,310
With your ability, can you keep up with me?

57
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:13,600
We won't know unless we try, right?

58
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:17,769
What does that mean?

59
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:22,310
I want to join too.

60
00:04:22,310 --> 00:04:24,570
To keep winning and keep moving forward,

61
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:27,030
to be able to defeat them,

62
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,600
relying on the three of us
to create a chemical reaction.

63
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:35,350
(Second Selection)

64
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:36,810
As you can see,

65
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:38,090
this second selection

66
00:04:38,090 --> 00:04:40,940
is honing interpersonal relationships,

67
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:41,960
(Japan Football Association)
strengthening self-awareness

68
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,300
(BL Manager, Anri Teieri)
and understanding others,

69
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:47,890
as well as forming teams
based on individual consideration.

70
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:50,800
Creating the world's best striker

71
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,850
who doesn't depend on others.

72
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:56,190
My report ends here.

73
00:04:56,190 --> 00:04:59,440
Sounds quite practical,

74
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,650
but in the end, it must rely on talent.

75
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:03,630
(Japan Football Association Advisor)
Even if geniuses are left alone,

76
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:05,570
(Hirotoshi Buratsuta)
they are still geniuses.

77
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:06,670
Right.

78
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:09,850
We need the next star
of the Japan representative team.

79
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:13,250
Quickly produce a genius high school student
who can shake the world.

80
00:05:13,250 --> 00:05:15,850
I just said, we're still at the second selection.

81
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:18,480
Are you so eager for a star?

82
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:22,920
A bunch of old men
who just want to make money.

83
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:26,400
Just how many geniuses
have you destroyed by now?

84
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,340
(Blue Lock Supreme Commander,
Jinpachi Ego)

85
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:31,600
What do you mean, Ego?

86
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:35,150
You always create
temporary geniuses,

87
00:05:35,150 --> 00:05:38,060
then those stupid fans
of the Japanese representative team

88
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:41,300
go crazy over the genius
at Japan's national standard

89
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:44,190
and spend loads of money
on jerseys and tickets.

90
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,600
That misunderstood genius

91
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,440
goes abroad without preparation

92
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:53,690
and because of cultural and language differences,
their performance is mediocre.

93
00:05:53,690 --> 00:05:56,480
A few years later,
after returning to Japan,

94
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:58,470
they are asked to join the domestic league

95
00:05:58,470 --> 00:06:00,920
and have an ordinary soccer career.

96
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:03,440
If this pattern keeps repeating,

97
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:07,270
Japanese soccer will forever
be third-rate.

98
00:06:07,270 --> 00:06:08,930
It's impossible to produce

99
00:06:08,930 --> 00:06:10,140
the world's best striker.

100
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:13,940
We must consider operational costs,

101
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:16,100
of course we have to try to make money.

102
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,230
Then let me ask you.

103
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,270
What is talent?

104
00:06:21,770 --> 00:06:24,480
An innate ability from birth?

105
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,740
Or a special physical capability?

106
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:32,230
To me, these are all just basics.

107
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:34,630
Listen carefully, talent is

108
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:37,830
the power to prove one's own strength.

109
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:40,650
A person who stakes their life

110
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:44,150
to prove and believe in their dream
in this world,

111
00:06:44,150 --> 00:06:47,170
I call that a genius.

112
00:06:47,170 --> 00:06:50,560
I want to create a genius
through Blue Lock.

113
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:54,150
This is my proof of staking my life.

114
00:06:56,970 --> 00:06:59,980
Is that so?
I'm really looking forward to it, Ego.

115
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,900
You must not fail.

116
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,190
This guy...

117
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:10,680
I've told him many times,

118
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,780
he's still sleeping in a single bunk.

119
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:15,350
I think I said we'd decide by rock-paper-scissors.

120
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:17,520
Can we wake him up?

121
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:22,710
However, the room became very tidy.

122
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:25,540
Did Servant Barou clean it?

123
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:26,940
Forget it then.

124
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:29,380
Thinking is such a hassle.

125
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:30,810
I'm going to sleep.

126
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:32,270
Is this okay?

127
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:34,350
Isn't this too careless? Honestly.

128
00:07:36,150 --> 00:07:38,520
In the end, I still sleep on the bottom bunk.

129
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,560
Geniuses really are so arbitrary.

130
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,770
Reo.

131
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:44,100
Okay.

132
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,770
Run, Chigiri.

133
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:46,770
Easy.

134
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,030
That shot just now was really good.

135
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:55,520
Great teamwork.

136
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,990
Your shots are truly beautiful, Young Lady.

137
00:07:56,990 --> 00:07:58,860
Probably, Isagi and the others

138
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:01,440
have already won a few stages
and reached the next phase, right?

139
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,840
If we don't hurry and catch up,

140
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,580
they'll have already finished it.

141
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,650
I understand,

142
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:10,260
but we still can't just randomly find teammates and win.

143
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:12,900
We have to improve our abilities,
then we can defeat Isagi.

144
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:14,930
Otherwise, we won't reach our goal.

145
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:16,470
However,

146
00:08:16,470 --> 00:08:19,650
aren't strong people winning and gathering
one by one in the next stage?

147
00:08:19,650 --> 00:08:21,940
That's true.

148
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:23,140
Reo, what do you think?

149
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:27,360
I just want to beat Nagi,
the rest doesn't matter.

150
00:08:27,810 --> 00:08:31,070
I want to make him say, "I need you."

151
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:32,700
You still haven't given up?

152
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:35,070
I want my revenge.

153
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:37,559
Good, so enthusiastic.

154
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:46,520
You are a genius with an amazing
adaptability skill.

155
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:50,020
Naruhaya called me that.

156
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:53,670
What is this adaptability skill?

157
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:56,240
At that time, I recreated Naruhaya's skill,

158
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:59,100
and got the win by entering the enemy's blind spot.

159
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:04,560
Does adaptability become stronger
by working together with an opponent?

160
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,060
If so,

161
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,910
the next opponent I need to adapt to is...

162
00:09:07,910 --> 00:09:08,810
Can I sit next to you?

163
00:09:08,810 --> 00:09:11,480
- this self-proclaimed king.
- Whatever.

164
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:16,560
For Barou, what is the ideal soccer style?

165
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:19,370
What kind of question is that?
Why are you asking?

166
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:23,020
I want to have some chemistry with you.

167
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,340
Because of that,

168
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:27,940
I think we need to understand
each other's soccer styles.

169
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,670
Tell me, what kind of soccer do you want to play?

170
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:37,180
Move so that I can score goals, that kind of thing.

171
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:42,020
But, we've already defeated that method.

172
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:45,600
Is there another way to better utilize teammates?

173
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,980
What nonsense is that?

174
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:50,530
If the Shorty moved according to my directions,

175
00:09:50,530 --> 00:09:51,820
we would have won from the start.

176
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:53,480
But we still lost in the end.

177
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,630
Even though you're really strong,

178
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,280
the whole team still couldn't win.

179
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,560
Who cares?

180
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,230
Anyway, we have to rely on my shooting to win.

181
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:02,990
My rules can't be changed.

182
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:07,020
If you want to rely on the team
to win so badly,

183
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:11,420
then you should have chosen
that Shorty as your teammate, Loser.

184
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,690
It's not like that!

185
00:10:12,690 --> 00:10:15,510
Maybe Naruhaya would understand
if I formed a team with him,

186
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:18,400
but he definitely couldn't trigger a chemical reaction.

187
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,770
(Blind Spot, Off the Ball)
I think this way

188
00:10:19,770 --> 00:10:21,100
because I've recreated his skill.

189
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,600
It's not enough with just the skills I can do.

190
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:26,690
A shooting range exceeding 28 meters

191
00:10:26,690 --> 00:10:28,230
and the ability to break through.

192
00:10:28,230 --> 00:10:30,640
You have abilities that I can't do,

193
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:33,190
even if I tried for a lifetime.

194
00:10:33,190 --> 00:10:37,150
With my presence, your talent will shine even brighter.

195
00:10:39,490 --> 00:10:42,950
Therefore, you should follow my orders even more.

196
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:44,020
Wait a minute.

197
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:47,020
If it's like this, there's no point in forming a team.

198
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,690
Shut up, I'm going to take a shower.

199
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:51,500
Annoying.

200
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,400
What's with that brat?

201
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,770
Where did such an arbitrary king come from?

202
00:10:55,770 --> 00:10:57,560
He must have very few friends,

203
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,230
no, probably none at all.

204
00:10:59,230 --> 00:11:00,340
Annoying.

205
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:04,770
His talent is indeed amazing,

206
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:07,900
but he won't win if he doesn't cooperate.

207
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:13,350
I've always felt that Barou
is a slightly unfortunate genius.

208
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,900
My muscles feel very sore,

209
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:23,350
is it because I trained physically with Barou?

210
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:26,900
He can do that kind of training every day.

211
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:29,770
Sorry, the bubbles are flying everywhere.

212
00:11:29,770 --> 00:11:31,350
Kunigami?

213
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:32,460
Isagi?

214
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:34,850
Why are you here?

215
00:11:34,850 --> 00:11:37,400
Shouldn't I be the one asking that?

216
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,940
Why are you still at the third stage?

217
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,720
In short,

218
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:47,100
you lost to Rin Itoshi
and had Bachira taken from you,

219
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:49,980
then you defeated Barou
and eliminated Naruhaya,

220
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:53,020
then finally appeared here, right?

221
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,810
More or less.

222
00:11:56,230 --> 00:11:58,980
Just because of a little carelessness,
you got into a difficult situation.

223
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:01,060
Who is Kunigami on a team with?

224
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:03,280
With me.

225
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,730
Why did you go off alone beforehand?

226
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:06,990
Isagi, you jerk.

227
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:08,120
Chigiri.

228
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,190
Jerk, why didn't you wait for me?

229
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:13,920
I feel the same way.

230
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:17,770
Sorry, originally I wanted to wait,

231
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:19,190
but Nagi wanted to team up with me.

232
00:12:19,190 --> 00:12:20,380
Are you talking about me?

233
00:12:22,730 --> 00:12:25,100
What are you doing?

234
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:29,180
A very relaxing way to bathe.

235
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:34,020
I would also accept
if Nagi wanted to team up with me.

236
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,770
I feel the same.

237
00:12:35,770 --> 00:12:37,850
Mr. Hassle.

238
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:40,600
What a jerk.

239
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:43,310
You can't soak in the public bath.

240
00:12:43,310 --> 00:12:45,820
It's fine, just for a little while.

241
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,030
Look, a ninja.

242
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,690
No releasing bubbles.

243
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:50,160
The public bath is full of your saliva.

244
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:53,250
You also enter the public bath
after cleaning your body, right?

245
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:56,270
It's been cleaned,
conditioner has also been used.

246
00:12:56,270 --> 00:12:58,850
The towel is very dirty, don't put it
into the public bath.

247
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:02,350
Isagi, is Barou someone
who's this detailed?

248
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:04,680
Yes, very detailed.

249
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,350
I'm a little dizzy, give me some water.

250
00:13:07,350 --> 00:13:09,650
Have you decided on an opponent
for the next match?

251
00:13:09,650 --> 00:13:11,930
No, not yet.
How about you?

252
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:13,730
We...

253
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,520
Of course against you guys.

254
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,690
I joined their team for this.

255
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:25,060
Reo, long time no see. Listen to me.

256
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:27,530
These past few days,
I've done a lot of training.

257
00:13:28,650 --> 00:13:33,200
No need to continue,
we are already opponents.

258
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:35,870
Because you didn't choose me,

259
00:13:36,310 --> 00:13:39,290
I will crush you here.

260
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:41,880
That's how it happened.

261
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:44,130
Let's have a match!

262
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:45,300
Don't even think about running away.

263
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:52,350
Good, that's what I was hoping for.

264
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:58,020
(Time Remaining Before the Match)

265
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:04,030
(Blue Lock)

266
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:09,070
Pass the ball to make it easier for Barou to act

267
00:14:09,070 --> 00:14:10,650
while watching the situation.

268
00:14:10,650 --> 00:14:13,020
Rely on my and Nagi's teamwork
to disrupt the opponent.

269
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,660
Finally, the goal scorer
is freely determined.

270
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:18,120
Okay. I think today
I can score a lot of goals.

271
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:20,290
Pass the ball to me.

272
00:14:20,290 --> 00:14:23,060
No way, you don't pass to me.

273
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,230
Still, you have to pass to me.

274
00:14:24,230 --> 00:14:25,010
No.

275
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:26,560
- Pass to me.
- I don't want to.

276
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,010
Getting those two to play
on the same soccer field

277
00:14:29,010 --> 00:14:30,220
is still really difficult.

278
00:14:30,730 --> 00:14:32,480
I can only try to adapt to them,

279
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,680
becoming the main actor
to trigger the chemical reaction.

280
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,590
Isagi, why did you agree

281
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:40,230
as soon as they provoked you?

282
00:14:40,230 --> 00:14:43,610
Actually, we could also play against other teams, right?

283
00:14:43,610 --> 00:14:48,030
Because... one of the reasons is
I don't want to be underestimated.

284
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:49,770
Nagi's curling shot skill,

285
00:14:49,770 --> 00:14:51,100
Barou's dribbling skill,

286
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:52,870
and my straight shot.

287
00:14:53,850 --> 00:14:55,690
Even though we have these skills,

288
00:14:55,690 --> 00:14:57,870
if we want to beat
the top three team led by Rin,

289
00:14:57,870 --> 00:15:01,270
I feel we're still missing
one crucial thing.

290
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:02,540
What's that?

291
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:05,090
Super-fast legs, Hyoma Chigiri.

292
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:08,170
I want his speed.

293
00:15:08,170 --> 00:15:09,680
I see.

294
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,240
Wait a minute.

295
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,930
Choose a post player who
can pass the ball to me.

296
00:15:13,930 --> 00:15:16,310
That orange-haired muscle guy,

297
00:15:16,310 --> 00:15:19,140
I want his "ball-holding skill".

298
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:20,690
What you say is true.

299
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:24,150
With Kunigami, the front line
is more capable of holding the ball.

300
00:15:24,150 --> 00:15:26,980
Besides, he also has
mid-range shooting ability.

301
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,320
After all, I still want to choose Reo.

302
00:15:29,850 --> 00:15:33,160
We promised each other
to be together until the end.

303
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,690
Wait, the players we want are different.

304
00:15:36,690 --> 00:15:40,060
Because I have a soccer style I want to play.

305
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:41,690
What does that matter?

306
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,630
There's no need to decide in a hurry now.

307
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:47,090
If we lose, one of us
will be taken anyway.

308
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:53,190
Alright. Let's confirm the formation again!

309
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:02,900
It's roughly like this: Reo is responsible
for the overall balance,

310
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:06,480
while Chigiri and I
attack them from left and right.

311
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:09,690
Okay, we've also confirmed the level
of team cooperation through training.

312
00:16:09,690 --> 00:16:12,490
In terms of destructive attacking power,
it's about half and half.

313
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:13,480
Yeah.

314
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:16,850
Next is deciding the target
each person marks.

315
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,080
I'll mark Yoichi Isagi.

316
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:22,580
I want to play soccer with him.

317
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:25,190
I'll block his movements

318
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:28,690
to prove that Nagi was wrong to choose him.

319
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,830
Alright, then physically speaking,

320
00:16:33,830 --> 00:16:35,340
I'll mark Barou.

321
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:37,350
In that case, I'll mark Nagi.

322
00:16:37,350 --> 00:16:39,940
Also, who do you want to take after we win?

323
00:16:40,930 --> 00:16:42,770
Isagi's skill

324
00:16:42,770 --> 00:16:44,270
will surely be amazing
if combined in this team.

325
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:46,730
Barou's individual ball technique is not bad either.

326
00:16:46,730 --> 00:16:49,070
However, ability-wise, I want Nagi.

327
00:16:49,070 --> 00:16:50,440
I feel the same way.

328
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,900
Even without much effort,
he's already that amazing.

329
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:56,020
Based on potential ability,
he's the only choice.

330
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,570
Is that okay, Reo?

331
00:16:57,570 --> 00:17:00,690
No, eliminate Nagi.

332
00:17:00,690 --> 00:17:04,290
Making him feel my feelings
isn't bad either.

333
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:07,650
Hey, don't put too much personal grudge into this.

334
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:09,880
This isn't your one-man soccer team.

335
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:13,980
Let's just take a vote
after the match ends.

336
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:17,800
After all, the answer lies within the match.

337
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:22,579
(Fourth Stage, Restaurant)

338
00:17:22,579 --> 00:17:23,890
Hey, you guys.

339
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:27,060
How about playing a match against me?

340
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:29,940
We want to challenge you, is that okay?

341
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:33,020
You're from the top three ranked, right?

342
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,400
Sorry for declining.

343
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,560
Come on, let's go!

344
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,240
Hold on a second.

345
00:17:37,770 --> 00:17:39,980
What number team is this now?

346
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,810
Everyone is scared and runs away.

347
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,020
What now?

348
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:46,370
(Current BL Rank 3rd, Aoshi Tokimitsu)

349
00:17:46,370 --> 00:17:48,810
Nobody wants to play a match against us.

350
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:50,840
What if our time runs out?

351
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,280
(Current BL Rank 2nd)
Those who managed to reach this stage

352
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,690
(Jyubei Aryu)
but are still running away,

353
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:55,100
it's not stylish at all.

354
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,590
Anyway, most likely
they'll be eliminated, right?

355
00:17:57,590 --> 00:17:58,600
(Current BL Rank 16th)
Honestly,

356
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:00,020
(Meguru Bachira)
I still don't want to play a match.

357
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:01,690
Isagi's group will definitely pass.

358
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:03,060
I want to wait for them.

359
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:07,190
But what if he doesn't pass?

360
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:08,730
It's over.

361
00:18:08,730 --> 00:18:12,230
Relax, Isagi will definitely come.

362
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:15,240
I can't lose again.

363
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:17,320
Isagi, let's advance!

364
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,530
Okay.

365
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:21,100
To get Bachira back,

366
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,480
I can't stop here.

367
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:29,710
Nice kick, Rin.

368
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:31,290
I want to join too.

369
00:18:31,290 --> 00:18:33,770
Just being a nuisance, get lost!

370
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:34,500
(Current BL Rank 1st, Rin Itoshi)

371
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:38,400
Are you playing soccer
to beat your older brother?

372
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,350
What about it?
Get out of my sight!

373
00:18:41,350 --> 00:18:43,060
It's the first time I've seen someone

374
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:45,890
play soccer as lonely as you.

375
00:18:46,690 --> 00:18:49,390
Are you trying to pick a fight, Kappa Head?

376
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:51,020
Play with me!

377
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:54,230
It will definitely be very fun.

378
00:18:56,310 --> 00:18:58,150
Chigiri.

379
00:18:58,150 --> 00:18:59,400
Does a hero

380
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,650
get fired up

381
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:03,490
when about to face a strong enemy?

382
00:19:03,490 --> 00:19:05,660
That's because you're on the same team as me,

383
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:06,950
Slow Hero.

384
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:09,900
We have to win, Chigiri.

385
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,380
Okay, Kunigami.

386
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:13,810
I will surpass everything.

387
00:19:16,090 --> 00:19:19,050
(Blue Lock, Second Selection
Rival Take-Match, Three-on-Three)

388
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:27,940
I wonder why?

389
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,850
I don't feel scared at all.

390
00:19:29,850 --> 00:19:33,020
Is it because I'm walking
alongside geniuses

391
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:36,440
or because... I've become stronger?

392
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:40,810
Let's prove it by winning this match.

393
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:49,980
Push forward, Barou!
Our chemical reaction is

394
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:52,270
the key to this match.

395
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:53,240
(Current BL Rank 50th)
Hey, King.

396
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,030
(Rensuke Kunigami)
Hey, King.

397
00:19:54,030 --> 00:19:56,420
I'm going to dethrone you.

398
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:57,780
(Current BL Rank 18th)
Just try it if you can,

399
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,980
(Shouei Barou)
Loser!

400
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:02,560
Do you think you can stop me?

401
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,520
Why? Your guarding is too loose.

402
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:08,720
If so, come at me.

403
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:12,770
What kind of guarding is that?

404
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:14,190
Sometimes closing in, sometimes backing away.

405
00:20:14,190 --> 00:20:15,900
What does he actually want?

406
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:18,980
Alright, it's up to you if you want to go that way.

407
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:22,900
Anyway, it's impossible for me
to completely stop you.

408
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,400
I see.

409
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:27,190
He doesn't intend to stop Barou
from dribbling outside.

410
00:20:27,190 --> 00:20:30,100
He's only stopping him from entering
the mid-range shooting zone.

411
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,750
A sturdy defender.

412
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:33,650
Utilizing Kunigami's physique,

413
00:20:33,650 --> 00:20:35,960
a guarding method specialized
for facing Barou.

414
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:39,170
But, I can only stop him up to this point.

415
00:20:39,170 --> 00:20:41,000
You're just a muscle-bound Loser.

416
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,590
Unexpectedly, you can think too.

417
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:44,380
Barou, pass here!

418
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,650
Shut up, don't piss me off!

419
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,760
I'll think of a way to break free from him!

420
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:51,150
He's really stubborn.

421
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:52,400
Isagi, what do we do?

422
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:55,190
Nagi, don't come here.
Wait for my instructions in the opponent's area.

423
00:20:55,190 --> 00:20:57,230
I'll help Barou keep moving forward.

424
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:59,350
What can you do if you go there?

425
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,900
Yoichi Isagi,
you've already realized, haven't you?

426
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:05,530
Nagi is a genius player I discovered.

427
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:06,550
(Current BL Rank 10th, Reo Mikage)

428
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:09,200
I must take him back from you
in this match.

429
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,240
(Current BL Rank 15th)
What's wrong with you?

430
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,160
(Yoichi Isagi)
What's wrong with you?

431
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,910
Barou, pass the ball! Now!

432
00:21:12,910 --> 00:21:14,410
Shut up, you're breaking my concentration!

433
00:21:14,410 --> 00:21:15,980
Hurry up and use me, Barou!

434
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,790
The King doesn't pass the ball.

435
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:21,130
Do you think you can beat us all alone?

436
00:21:21,130 --> 00:21:22,460
Reo, you're too slow.

437
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,560
Thanks for holding on, Muscle Wall.

438
00:21:25,510 --> 00:21:27,260
Damn!

439
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:29,100
See, didn't I tell you?

440
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:29,980
Come on, Kunigami!

441
00:21:29,980 --> 00:21:31,140
I already ran!

442
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:33,100
Are these guys for real?

443
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,810
They cornered Barou together
because they know he won't pass.

444
00:21:35,810 --> 00:21:38,190
Also, the switching between defense
and offense is so fast!

445
00:21:38,190 --> 00:21:40,150
I won't be able to handle

446
00:21:40,150 --> 00:21:41,860
Reo and Kunigami all alone.

447
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:44,820
But, I have to stop them
as the last line of defense.

448
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:46,600
Will he dribble through
the defensive line

449
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:48,480
or pass to Kunigami?

450
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,530
What will he do?

451
00:21:49,530 --> 00:21:51,190
I'll wait until the very last second,

452
00:21:51,190 --> 00:21:53,690
keep the timing to react,

453
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:56,580
and see the moment Reo chooses!

454
00:21:59,190 --> 00:22:00,440
Kunigami!

455
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:02,400
I just need to stop this pass.

456
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,520
He's passing the ball...

457
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,440
to Chigiri!

458
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,100
(BL Rank 44th, Hyoma Chigiri)

459
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:12,220
So accurate, Reo!

460
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:16,020
You've gotten slower because of stopping, haven't you?

461
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:17,560
(Current BL Rank 7th)
I've caught up to you,

462
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:18,900
(Seishiro Nagi)
Red Leopard.

463
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:20,370
You only managed to catch me for a moment.

464
00:22:20,370 --> 00:22:21,900
Happy with just that, Genius?

465
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:23,020
In that case,

466
00:22:25,070 --> 00:22:27,450
keep staying in my shadow!

467
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:32,440
Are you serious?
This is my first time marking him.

468
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:35,580
He's so fast it's making me angry.

469
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:37,270
Our formation

470
00:22:37,270 --> 00:22:39,040
has been completely broken by them!

471
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:40,650
Kunigami's physique,

472
00:22:40,650 --> 00:22:42,060
Reo's tactical eye,

473
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:44,590
and Chigiri's super-fast legs.

474
00:22:44,690 --> 00:22:47,220
The three of them understand
each other's skills

475
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:49,310
and bring out each other's capabilities.

476
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:52,260
That's why they can outperform
the two geniuses, Barou and Nagi!

477
00:22:52,260 --> 00:22:54,970
This is the "three-person chemical reaction"
at the highest level!

478
00:22:59,730 --> 00:23:01,900
Great!

479
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:03,730
Damn!

480
00:23:04,190 --> 00:23:05,940
A very strong team,

481
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:09,320
it makes my fighting spirit burn.

482
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:12,940
It makes me want to crush them!

483
00:23:14,650 --> 00:23:18,040
Blue Lock Extra Scene!

484
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,540
(#16 King Barou's Maid Cafe)
Welcome back home, Master!

485
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:23,000
(Barou)
Barou, Barou, chu!

486
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:23,720
(King Barou)

487
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:26,520
King Barou's special love omelet rice,

488
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:29,270
full of love!

489
00:23:29,270 --> 00:23:31,600
Barou, Barou, chu!

490
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:32,760
Chu!

491
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:35,770
(Isagi) (Nagi)
Wasn't Servant Barou supposed to be like that?

492
00:23:35,770 --> 00:23:38,350
Oh my god. That's really ridiculous, you know?

493
00:23:38,350 --> 00:23:41,560
(Shouei Barou)
Don't carelessly imagine things, Trash!

494
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,850
That wasn't bad just now.

495
00:23:43,850 --> 00:23:45,850
A curt cafe maid.

496
00:23:45,850 --> 00:23:47,480
You're right.

497
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,140
(King Barou the Curt Cafe Maid)

498
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:50,070
Welcome back home,

499
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:52,310
You Pile of Trash!

500
00:23:54,070 --> 00:23:56,440
Something like this might be popular.

501
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,150
A good chance to make lots of money!

502
00:23:58,150 --> 00:23:59,160
Not bad.

503
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:01,830
Don't! Watch it, I'll kill you!